{"title":"2010 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as its incenter and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> as its circumcircle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4057c3e63298c2ed6715003afb6f2d9dc6272037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDC$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> a point on the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0f4d822f936fbbfaa8700200027e1be4419c6d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAF=\\angle CAE&lt; \\frac12\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"227\" height=\"37\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/6987ce01cfbd8256d13f69583906c05b4481cb8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IF$\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" />, prove that the intersection of lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f506b80246907627b4826e4d0fddd0a15f5913c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EI$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf9409044fef7f3966027eec40b2cced52eb16c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DG$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><i>Authors: Tai Wai Ming and Wang Chongli, Hong Kong</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that it suffices to prove alternatively that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f506b80246907627b4826e4d0fddd0a15f5913c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EI$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> meets the circle again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f1176c98ab387e4277c96ff77b352f24b4ec6b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JD$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/6987ce01cfbd8256d13f69583906c05b4481cb8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IF$\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/6987ce01cfbd8256d13f69583906c05b4481cb8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IF$\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f1176c98ab387e4277c96ff77b352f24b4ec6b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JD$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Observation 1. D is the midpoint of arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4057c3e63298c2ed6715003afb6f2d9dc6272037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDC$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> because it lies on angle bisector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Observation 2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d7156c8b5b86df59e4974e175ad2cff8c5a307fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{FAE}$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> as well.\n</p><p>Key Lemma. Triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/fae05c9a5faa2819b127bd4dced25fa468fc11f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DKI$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/525d157149e2bc6ac6713b5c819c285bbd042e4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DIJ$\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" /> are similar.\nProof. Because triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1c810f39fdd8e75e63154512252f162c8eb8da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DKB$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/f/b9ff0fb1f3bf1a8bb6183f1e6ca2b57e86cce923.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBJ$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> are similar by AA Similarity (for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d094817188aa7d4a404ba1f4420884f75b13dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{KBD}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/139906772df062c736cd4a447f92d5d7345f556f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BJD}$\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" /> both intercept equally sized arcs), we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cef5bfc738d93ff7b2eb563aa93f1380adcba572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD^2 = BK \\cdot BJ$\" width=\"133\" height=\"15\" />. But we know that triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da39cfc4135f88e4478e2615258184e749bb945a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBI$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> is isosceles (hint: prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/484348abae0ffc5a17b660445e8ce0acb8557e99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BID} = \\angle{IBD}$\" width=\"128\" height=\"12\" />), and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7642e9c010570c0ae443a70e7f8b2e5afebd05a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BI^2 = BK \\cdot BJ$\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" />. Hence, by SAS Similarity, triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/fae05c9a5faa2819b127bd4dced25fa468fc11f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DKI$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/525d157149e2bc6ac6713b5c819c285bbd042e4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DIJ$\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" /> are similar, as desired.\n</p><p>Observation 3. As a result, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4ca863b41e5345c54fca8e60ff361f905b5f39a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{KID} = \\angle{IJD} = \\angle{DAE} = \\angle{FAD}$\" width=\"289\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Observation 4. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/e/33e4fdd5db309bc0598384b51bcc79622421bf32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IK // AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Observation 5. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f1176c98ab387e4277c96ff77b352f24b4ec6b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JD$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/a/dfac16283acf9a3e23d0d398f3c8521d3d3dd7db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJLI$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> is cyclic.\n</p><p>Observation 6. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/1/ca133361dd2a9ec73fbb8eac0eba98974b3d1fb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ALI} = \\angle{AJE} = \\angle{AJC} + \\angle{CJE} = \\angle{B} + \\angle{AEC} = \\angle{B} + \\angle{BAF} = \\angle{AFC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"615\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/deedbf659ccbfb88ab004eebe4d65aee3432078a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LI // FK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Observation 7. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/806b584026332ab062427f0a9625b1755aefff3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LIKF$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> is a parallelogram, so its diagonals bisect each other, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb47261bdfc683fe04c09798101fd8ae59c5ece4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2010_IMO_2.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/fd/2010_IMO_2.png/330px-2010_IMO_2.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"330\" height=\"322\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/fd/2010_IMO_2.png/495px-2010_IMO_2.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/fd/2010_IMO_2.png/660px-2010_IMO_2.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> be A-excenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee0b3f67c82d03d07b6dbbe1220570cddf2f85f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"97\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b3460bfb01d88880906778e990654e0420eb68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DI = DB = DC = DA&#39;, AB \\cdot AC = AI \\cdot AA&#39;.\\]\" width=\"364\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e172fc5f35e15422ca5a78fd37b6da920971afac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BAF = \\angle EAC, \\angle ABF = \\angle ABC = \\angle AEC \\implies \\triangle ABF \\sim \\triangle AEC \\implies\\]\" width=\"585\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f537acce151eccc59e57337cc2891685cfcccb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {AB}{AF} = \\frac {AE}{AC} \\implies AF \\cdot AE = AB \\cdot AC = AI \\cdot AA&#39; \\implies \\frac {AF}{AA&#39;} = \\frac {AI}{AE}.\\]\" width=\"536\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/6/5060840af51d72f69c1b0d5f5d394cf7be25634a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle FAA&#39; = \\angle IAE \\implies \\triangle FAA&#39; \\sim \\triangle IAE \\implies \\angle FA&#39;A = \\angle IEA.\\]\" width=\"509\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b4a780c3a685662e5d391f9387c2c753c95d5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[IG = GF, ID = DA&#39; \\implies GD || FA&#39; \\implies \\angle GDA = \\angle FA&#39;A = \\angle IEA \\implies\\]\" width=\"589\" height=\"18\" />\nthe intersection of lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f506b80246907627b4826e4d0fddd0a15f5913c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EI$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf9409044fef7f3966027eec40b2cced52eb16c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DG$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>After <i><b>pavel kozlov</b></i> <b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO\" title=\"2010 IMO\">2010 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2010 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017223400\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 354/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10799/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.440      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.440      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8845:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017223400 and revision id 195804. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}